.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-server-disk-add - Add an additional disk


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro server disk add  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add an additional disk

.PP
Two classes: \fBssd\fR (fast) and \fBhdd\fR (large storage for backups, archives and media; do not run databases on it). Additional disks are billed per GB hourly from the prepaid balance (\fBclasses.<class>.per_gb_monthly_eur\fR, monthly / 672), from the hour they are added until they are removed; each disk at least \fBpricing.minimum_hours\fR\&. Up to 4 disks per server and \fBclasses.<class>.max_gb\fR GB per class; sizes are multiples of \fBstep_gb\fR\&. A new disk is empty (partition, format and mount it inside the server). Reinstalling the server removes the additional disks. Prepaid tr-ist-1 servers only; not while the server is suspended.

.PP
API: POST /cloud/servers/{id}/disks (operationId addServerDisk, scope cloud_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--class\fP=""
	ssd (fast) or hdd (large storage; see classes.hdd.on_sale) (ssd|hdd)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
